<DocsLayout title="CrewAI guide | Agent-Gantry" description="Integrate Agent-Gantry with CrewAI: selected BaseTools, failures as CrewAI ToolFailure, approval through a before_tool_call hook, and agent/task context.">
  <p class="eyebrow">Framework guide</p>
  <h1>CrewAI</h1>
  <p class="lead">Agent-Gantry hands each CrewAI agent only the tools relevant to its task, as native <code>BaseTool</code>s. Failures come back as CrewAI's own <code>ToolFailure</code>, confirmation-gated tools go through a <code>before_tool_call</code> hook, and tools can read the agent, task and crew they are running for.</p>
  <p><a class="pill" href="/Agent-Gantry/docs/frameworks/crewai/advanced/">Advanced CrewAI usage →</a></p>

  <h2>Install</h2>
  <CodeBlock lang="bash" code={`uv add "agent-gantry[crewai]"   # crewai >= 1.15.22, Python 3.10-3.13`} />
  <div class="callout"><strong>Separate from the OpenAI Agents SDK:</strong> CrewAI pins <code>openai&lt;3</code>, while <code>openai-agents</code> 0.23 and later need <code>openai&gt;=3</code>, so the two extras cannot share an environment.</div>

  <h2>Basic page: select tools per agent</h2>
  <CodeBlock lang="python" code={`from crewai import Agent, Crew, Task
from agent_gantry import AgentGantry
from agent_gantry.crewai import CrewAIAdapter

gantry = AgentGantry()

@gantry.register(examples=["where is my order", "has order 4471 shipped"])
def get_order_status(order_id: str) -> str:
    """Return the current shipping status for an order."""
    return "in_transit"

await gantry.sync()
adapter = CrewAIAdapter(gantry)
query = "Has order 4471 shipped?"
agent = Agent(role="support", goal="Answer order questions", backstory="...",
              tools=await adapter.select(query, limit=3))
task = Task(description=query, expected_output="A short answer", agent=agent)
result = await Crew(agents=[agent], tasks=[task]).kickoff_async()`} />
  <p>CrewAI fixes an agent's tools when it is built. To re-select per task, use <code>adapter.agent_builder(role=..., llm=...)</code> and call <code>await builder.build(query)</code> before each one.</p>

  <h2>What the agent sees when a tool fails</h2>
  <p>A failed call returns CrewAI's <code>ToolFailure</code> with the error type as its <code>code</code>. The agent reads the message, capped at 2,000 characters, and CrewAI records the failure on <code>TaskOutput.tool_failures</code>. Set <code>tool_failure_policy="raise"</code> on the agent or task to abort instead.</p>
  <div class="callout"><strong>Redact or opt out:</strong> <code>CrewAIAdapter(gantry, error_formatter=redact)</code> rewrites the text; <code>error_mode="raise"</code> lets <code>ToolExecutionError</code> propagate into CrewAI's own exception handling.</div>
</DocsLayout>
